.TH WMTHEME 2
.SH NAME
wmtheme \- the window system's own colours
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "wmtheme.m";
wmtheme := load Wmtheme Wmtheme->PATH;

Inactive, Focused, Chrome, Glyph, Label, Desktop: con iota;
Ncolour: con Desktop+1;

init: fn();
rgba: fn(i: int): int;
hex:  fn(i: int): string;
set:  fn(i, rgba: int);
name: fn(i: int): string;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Wmtheme
holds the colours the window system draws its own furniture with.
.PP
It is not a palette a program picks from.
These are the specific things the chrome is made of \(em the titlebar of
a window that has the keyboard and of one that does not, its buttons, the
artwork on them, the title's text, and what is behind every window \(em
and a theme is a different set of values for exactly these names.
.TP
.B rgba
The colour packed for
.IR draw (2).
.TP
.B hex
The same colour as
.BR #rrggbb ,
which is what
.IR tk (2)
takes.
The alpha is dropped; every colour here is opaque.
.TP
.B set
Change one.
Widgets already made keep the colour they were made with, so this is for
setting a theme before windows exist rather than for changing one under
a running system.
.SS Why not grpalette(2)
.IR Grpalette (2)
is TempleOS's sixteen-colour register, where a colour
.I is
an index into a table that a program rewrites underneath a finished
drawing.
These are specific values, and routing them through sixteen slots would
either change them or bolt custom entries onto a fixed table.
The right shape, the wrong table.
.SS What it replaced
Four colours in
.B /appl/lib/titlebar.b
written out fourteen times, three more in
.B /appl/lib/wmclient.b
as constants, and the desktop background written twice \(em in
.B wmclient.b
and in
.B /appl/wm/wm.b
\(em which a comment in the first of them described as unavoidable
because there was no shared home for it.
.PP
The defaults are exactly the values that were there, so adopting this
changed no pixel.
.IR Tkofftest (1)
holds that to both ends: that the register still holds what was written
down before, and that the titlebar on the page is the colour the register
says.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/wmtheme.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR wm (1),
.IR tkclient (2),
.IR grpalette (2),
.B /doc/ui-next-plan.md
.SH BUGS
Programs that draw their own furniture \(em
.B /appl/wm/sweeper.b
and
.B /appl/wm/vt.b
have their own colours \(em are not covered.
.PP
There is no way to load a theme from a file, so a different set of values
means a program calling
.B set
before it makes any window.
